--  Replacing a running process with a new version of its program (ADR
--  0032, section 1, #866). Mem serves it, and only init has it: init's
--  install path, the update boot's installer, and the install's run of
--  the self tests (the Replace_Process role).
--
--  Replace_Process starts the replacement of the process that Old names,
--  which is any cap to one of its objects, such as its Replaceable: it
--  holds the process's calls, and returns the replacement, which the
--  caller drives (Replacement). The null cap if Old names no process
--  that mem launched, a replacement is in progress already, or a
--  checkpoint is.
--
--  Mem doesn't call Old to test that the process is Replaceable: a call
--  could wait for a page fault that mem has to serve. A process that
--  isn't Replaceable can't be taken over, so the new version's launch
--  fails, and the replacement can't commit.

interface Replacer is

   function Replace_Process
     (Old : Capability)
     return interface Replacement;

end Replacer;
